course: dictionary
lesson: 14139
title: Words for wrong ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A misapprehension is a wrong idea about something, a misunderstanding. It is a formal word, so you will meet it more in books and school work than in everyday chat. «She was under the misapprehension that the shop was open, so she walked all the way there.» Her idea was wrong, so she had a misapprehension.
explain: Look at the start of the word. Mis- means wrong, as in «misread» and «misspell». So when you see mis- at the front, ask yourself what has gone wrong. Then check the sentence to see whether an idea in it is false.
explain: In science, a misapprehension is like a misconception. Many people have the misapprehension that heavy things always fall faster than light things. Tests and experiments help us to change a wrong idea like that. In a story, a misapprehension tells the reader that a character believes something untrue, so the reader may know more than the character does.
fact: A misapprehension is a wrong idea or a misunderstanding about something.
fact: «Misapprehension» is a formal word, so it is common in books and school work.
fact: The prefix mis- means wrong, as in «misread» and «misspell».
fact: «Under the misapprehension that...» means believing something that is not true.
fact: A misunderstanding is a simpler word with a similar meaning, but misapprehension sounds more formal.
exercise: «Under the misapprehension that the library was open, Mia cycled all the way there.» What is the misapprehension here? | A fast bicycle | A library book about bikes | A map of the town | *A wrong idea that the library was open
exercise: What does the mis- in misapprehension mean? | Happy | Again | *Wrong | Very big
exercise: Which one is a misapprehension? | Knowing that the sun rises in the east | Having a bath before bed | *Believing heavy things always fall faster than light things, when they do not | Reading a book quietly
test: «Ravi had the misapprehension that the match was cancelled, so he stayed at home.» What was Ravi's misapprehension? | The match was cancelled | The match was too long | He was going to the match | *He believed the match was cancelled, when it was not
test: Which word means a wrong idea or a misunderstanding? | *Misapprehension | Instruction | Evidence | Certainty
exam: «Under the misapprehension that the bus had gone, Jo walked home, but the bus was still waiting.» What does misapprehension mean here? | *A wrong belief that the bus had gone | A happy feeling about walking home | A clear and correct plan | A ticket for the bus
